<title>UK: CRICKET-AUSTRALIA ON TOP OF THE WORLD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-AUSTRALIA ON TOP OF THE WORLD.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia have confirmed their place on top of the cricketing world after clinching the series against West Indies on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Australia's victory by an innings and 183 runs in Adelaide to lead 3-1 in the five-test rubber put them clear at the top of the Wisden world championship. Previously they shared the lead with South Africa and West Indies.</p>
<p>The championship, devised by Wisden Cricketers' Almanack, is unofficial, but South Africa intend to propose at the International Cricket Council (ICC) meeting in June that an official championship based on the Wisden system should be instituted.</p>
<p>Rankings are based on the most recent meetings, both home and away, between each pair of teams, with two points for winning each series or one-off test and one for drawing. The difference between the number played and points decides placings.</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, points, difference)</p>
<p> Australia		14    21     +7</p>
<p> South Africa	   12    17     +5</p>
<p> India		    13    17     +4</p>
<p> West Indies	    11    14     +3</p>
<p> Pakistan		 12    14     +2</p>
<p> Sri Lanka		14    12     -2</p>
<p> England		  14    11     -3</p>
<p> Zimbabwe		 10     4     -6</p>
<p> New Zealand	    16     6    -10</p>
